//This file only contains strings relevant to the installation of the mod

@-1004="PLEASE report the error message in the file"

@100010=~This component requires Baldur's Gate II: Enhanced Edition or Enhanced Edition Trilogy (EET).~
@100011=~This component requires an Enhanced Edition of Baldur's Gate: BG:EE, BG2:EE or EET.~
@100012=~Item Randomiser's own version of this component is installed. Keep that one, or uninstall it before installing this one.~

@101500=~Chriz Item Randomiser: randomises items anew for each new adventure (requires EEex with LuaJIT)~
@101501=~This component requires Baldur's Gate: Enhanced Edition, Baldur's Gate II: Enhanced Edition or Enhanced Edition Trilogy (EET).~
@101502=~This component requires EEex. Please install EEex first.~
@101503=~Chriz Item Randomiser cannot be combined with Item Randomiser's randomisation (Mode 1 or Mode 2).~
@101504=~Chriz Item Randomiser cannot be combined with Item Randomiser's "More Spell Shield scrolls"; its configurator offers that option for each adventure.~
@101505=~Another copy of this randomiser's runtime (override/M_FLPR.lua) is installed, for example Item Randomiser's component 1500. Please uninstall it before installing this component.~
@101506=~A DLC archive (sod-dlc.zip, or a ZIP file in the dlc folder) is not merged into the game. WeiDU cannot read it, so this component would hide the DLC's own menus and new-game template. Merge the DLC first, for example with DLC Merger, then install this component. Installation stopped.~
@101510=~This component requires the EEex LuaJIT component: InfinityLoader.ini must contain exactly one LuaPatchMode line, LuaPatchMode=REPLACE_INTERNAL_WITH_EXTERNAL. Installation stopped.~
@101512=~The user interface (UI.MENU and the other menu and Lua files) has no single-player New Game call (startEngine:OnNewGameButtonClick) or no character acceptance call (createCharScreen:AcceptCharacter). Installation stopped.~
@101513=~BALDUR.GAM is missing or is not a new-game template of an Enhanced Edition game (GAME V2.0, V2.1 or V1.1). Installation stopped.~
@101514=~BALDUR.GAM already defines the global FLPR_FRESH more than once or with a value other than 1. Installation stopped.~
@101515=~%flir_rt_file%, line %flir_rt_line%: "%flir_rt_form%" uses New Game, character import or character acceptance in a way this component cannot redirect; it can redirect calls such as startEngine:OnNewGameButtonClick(). Please report this message with your list of mods. Installation stopped.~
@101516=~%flir_rt_file%, line %flir_rt_line% already calls the FLPRUI_ functions this component adds, although it is not installed; uninstalling it would leave those calls without their functions. Installation stopped.~
@101520=~Note: Chriz Item Randomiser cannot prepare %flir_cp_name%, because %flir_cp_reason%. It stays as installed, and the configurator will not offer what depends on it.~
@101521=~the game has no such file~
@101522=~it already contains changes from an earlier version of this randomiser~
@101523=~it no longer gives the reward~
@101524=~it gives the reward more than once~
@101525=~it gives the reward in an unexpected way~
@101526=~it no longer takes the quest item~
@101527=~its journal entries have an unexpected form~
@101528=~the conversation has an unexpected form~

@109000=~Cespenar can forge SoA items~
@109001=~Note: Cespenar already has a recipe that uses Red Dragon scales in this game, so this component adds none for them.~
@109002=~Note: Cespenar already has a recipe that uses Shadow Dragon scales in this game, so this component adds none for them.~
@110000=~Remove Protection from Undead scrolls from stores~
@110100=~All scrolls from all stores~
@110200=~All scrolls from 9 out of 10 stores~
@110201=~No store sells scrolls of Protection from Undead (SCRL09), so nothing was changed.~
@110202=~Removed the scrolls of Protection from Undead from %flir_tw_removed% of the %flir_tw_selling% stores that sold them.~
@110203=~Note: these files could not be read as stores and were left as they are:%flir_tw_unreadable%~
@110210=~Duergar merchants~
@110300=~Prevent Watcher's Keep statues from disappearing~
@110301=~Note: AR3001.BCS has no difficulty adjustment that removes the Watcher's Keep statues (another mod may have changed it), so nothing was changed.~
@110302=~Note: another mod has already stopped AR3001.BCS from removing the Watcher's Keep statues for a small or weak party, so nothing was changed.~
@110303=~Note: %flir_tw_other% script block(s) of AR3001.BCS destroy a Watcher's Keep statue for reasons of their own; they stay as they are.~
